# Everything derived from or belonging to the user's own copy of the game lives
# under private/: the executable, the installation, the Proton prefix, captures,
# fixtures, the analyzer's function map, the lifted C, build output, venvs.
# No trailing slash: with one, the pattern matches a directory but not a symlink
# of the same name, so a stray link could be committed and replace the real
# directory on the next checkout. That happened once in reference-project.
/private
/build
/.venv

# Agent harness state (settings, worktrees, transcripts) stays local. The one tracked
# entry is the skills link to .agents/skills.
/.claude/*
!/.claude/skills

# Compiler output anywhere in the tree. `ship.py` stages with `git add -A`, so
# an object file left in the repository root by a probe build is one command
# away from being committed -- which nearly happened on 2026-09-21, when a
# unit compiling `runtime/sa2_dialog.c` wrote `sa2_dialog.o` beside it. The
# boundary rule (design 12.9) says never commit build output; this makes it
# true by default rather than by everyone remembering.
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.obj

# Editor and Python debris.
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
*~
*.swp
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/

# Game frames, video and recorded streams stay under private/.
*.y4m
*.y4m.times.tsv
*.mp4
*.i420
*.bgra
*.sa2s
*.sa2s.status
*.sa2d3d9
frame-[0-9]*.png
*_d3d9.log

# Claude Code session state.
/.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# Local run logs and distribution archives.
*.jsonl
*.apk
*.zip
*.7z
